description: Keep scraper/source references brand-neutral in code and docs
alwaysApply: true
---

# Neutral references to the scraper source

- Do **not** name the upstream music streaming service, its parent company, or related product names in comments, strings, README, env examples, commit messages, or user-facing copy.
- Prefer generic wording: **source site**, **upstream**, **catalog API**, **SCRAPER_SOURCE_BASE_URL**, **scraper source**.
- Technical API parameters required for compatibility (e.g. query keys, client context tokens) may stay as-is when they are not readable brand names.
